    <tr>
      <td class="abe-column-block-padding" id="abe-column-block-2b90d051-34f1-4be7-adae-02aa33df2aa7-padding" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt; padding: 15px;">
<img class="govd_template_image" src="https://content.govdelivery.com/attachments/fancy_images/OHCCC/2022/08/6307105/email-headers-updates-on-programs_original.png" style="width: 570px; height: auto; -ms-interpolation-mode: bicubic; line-height: 1; outline: none; text-decoration: none; max-width: 100%; border: none;" alt="Updates and Information on Programs" width="570" height="98"><h1 style="line-height: 1.2; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 24px; color: #00539B; margin: 0.67em 0 20px;">Senior Programming Discussions: What We Heard</h1>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;">Dear Resident,</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;">Thank you to everyone who attended the Senior Programming and Updates discussions over the past several weeks. More than 250 residents joined the conversation — and your input was thoughtful, solution-focused and incredibly helpful.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;">Across all five sessions, several clear themes emerged:</p>
<ul style="margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 15px;">
<li style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin-top: 0px;">
<strong>Protect core programs, especially fitness.</strong> Classes such as stretching, yoga, line dancing and strength training were consistently described as essential. Technology and computer classes, field trips and creative programs like quilting and ceramics are also highly valued.</li>
<li style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467;">
<strong>Maintain a mix of free and paid classes, with modest and gradual increases.</strong> Many shared that small, incremental adjustments feel more manageable than significant changes.</li>
<li style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467;">
<strong>Ensure affordability for those on fixed incomes.</strong> Suggested solutions included sliding-scale fees, scholarships, age- or income-based pricing and payment plans to spread out costs.</li>
<li style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467;">
<strong>Explore membership or bundle options.</strong> Many residents expressed interest in simplified pricing, such as a membership model or discounts for enrolling in multiple classes.</li>
<li style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin-bottom: 15px;">
<strong>Look for creative ways to offset costs without increasing class fees.</strong> Ideas included pursuing grants, leveraging partnerships, increasing rental rates and expanding volunteer instructor support.</li>
</ul>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;">You also brought several questions to the meetings. Below are the questions that came up regularly in case you didn't catch the answer.</p>
<h2 style="line-height: 1.2; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 22px; color: #00539B; margin: 0 0 18px;"><strong>Next Steps</strong></h2>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;">Our team is carefully reviewing all feedback and evaluating options to ensure seniors can continue accessing the programs that matter most while maintaining sustainable operations. We will continue this work through the spring and plan to share a proposal no later than June. Any changes would take effect no earlier than this fall.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;">Thank you again for showing up, speaking up and helping shape the future of senior programming. Your voices matter, and we are listening!</p>
<h2 align="left" style="line-height: 1.2; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 22px; color: #00539B; margin: 0 0 18px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>Q: What kind of influence does our feedback actually have?</strong></p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>A:</strong> Your participation at the December commission meeting directly led to these feedback sessions. Because of your engagement, planned changes were paused so we could hear from you first. These forums exist because you spoke up—your voices are shaping the next steps.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>Q: Why do we need to raise prices now?</strong></p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>A:</strong> Just like for families, cost increases are affecting the department. It costs us more to operate our facilities, run our programs and hire staff. Despite those cost increases, we are committed to continue providing quality programs. </p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;">To ensure the sustainability of our programs and facilities, we’re working to better align program fees with the actual cost of offering programs. We’re also working to make pricing more consistent across all centers – some centers already charge fees, while others do not. This update would streamline pricing citywide.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;">That means introducing fees for some classes that were previously free, particularly those with paid instructors. <strong>Important clarification:</strong> Fees would be <strong>per session</strong>, not per class; for example, if you sign up for a line dancing class that meets every Monday and Wednesday during the 8-week session, you would pay the registration fee <strong>one time, not every Monday and Wednesday</strong>.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>Q: How were these decisions made?</strong></p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>A:</strong> We reviewed all program areas, cost trends and participation data. We also examined fees in comparable cities. The goal was a balanced, fair approach that protects access for the greatest number of residents.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>Q: Didn’t you just get money from the bond package that passed in November?</strong></p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>A:</strong> The bond package covers future investments in our facilities, and can’t be used to support programming. <a href="https://www.columbus.gov/Government/Bonds?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; color: #9D4359;">Learn more about the bond package and what the money is intended for</a>.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>Q: How do Columbus’ fees compare to other communities?</strong></p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>A:</strong> Even with these adjustments, Columbus Recreation and Parks remains one of the most affordable systems in the region.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>Q: Why can’t instructors or centers fundraise to replace the fee increases?</strong></p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>A:</strong> Fundraising is voluntary and cannot reliably cover recurring operating expenses. Sustainable, predictable funding is necessary to keep programs consistent, safe and staffed.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;">The department is working with the Columbus Recreation and Parks Foundation to increase efforts to fundraise and secure sponsorships and partnerships to support programs and the PLAY Scholarship Fund. With a new team in place, we’re hopeful we can increase donations.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>Q: Are instructors earning more because of these increases?</strong></p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>A:</strong> Program fees support the cost of running the program — staffing, supplies and specialized training. Individual instructor pay is not tied to these fee adjustments.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>Q: Could fees go up again in the future?</strong></p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>A:</strong> We strive to keep fees stable, and any future adjustments would go through the same careful review. Our priority is affordability and access for the entire community.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>Q: What if residents simply can’t afford the fee increases?</strong></p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>A:</strong> Staff are available to talk through alternative programs, low-cost options and ways to stay connected to recreation, fitness and community activities without added financial strain.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>Q: Do SilverSneakers and other insurance programs cover access to fitness classes?</strong></p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>A: </strong>All community centers partner with SilverSneakers, Silver &amp; Fit, Active &amp; Fit and Renew Active. These programs provide access to the fitness room and all adult open sports activities. When you scan your Leisure Card upon entry, those visits are tracked and the department is reimbursed. Coverage does not automatically apply to all instructor-led classes.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>Q: Are SilverSneakers and other insurance programs only offered through Medicaid?</strong></p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>A: </strong>These programs are offered through multiple insurance programs. Check with your insurance provider to see if you have access. <a href="https://columbusrecparks.com/wellness/fitness/insurance/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; color: #9D4359;">Check out which program is available at your local community center</a>.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>Q: Why are prices being raised when we already pay property taxes?</strong></p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>A:</strong> Columbus Recreation and Parks is funded primarily through city income tax, not property tax. Property taxes also support other park systems, such as Metro Parks. Our department receives about 75 percent of its operating budget from income tax, with the rest coming from fees and other sources.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;">To put it in context: Columbus Recreation and Parks represents about 4–5 percent of the total city budget, while public safety accounts for roughly 80 percent. Our team maintains and operates more than 450 parks, 28 community centers, eight outdoor pools and other facilities across the city.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>Q: Does Columbus Recreation and Parks have an advocate at the city level?</strong></p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>A:</strong> Yes. The department is supported by the Recreation and Parks Commission and city leadership. Budget decisions are competitive across all departments, and community advocacy plays a major role. Residents are among our strongest and most effective advocates.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>Q: What do the Recreation and Parks Commissioners do?</strong></p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>A:</strong> The Recreation and Parks Commission is appointed under the City Charter and is responsible for overseeing and approving legislation related to parks and recreation facilities. The commission does not manage day-to-day operations and does not approve the department’s budget.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>Q: When would any price changes take effect?</strong></p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>A:</strong> Feedback from these sessions will be reviewed before any decisions are finalized. If approved, changes would take effect in fall 2026.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>Q: How can I see where the department’s funds are spent? </strong></p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 14px; color: #636467; margin: 0 0 15px;"><strong>A: </strong><a href="https://columbusrecparks.com/connect/about/press-room/?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; color: #9D4359;">The department’s annual report is posted on the website each spring</a>. </p>
</td>
